          %title Related entries
          %p This page concerns:
          %ul
            %li
              %p Alessandra Capotosti:
              %p
                %br/
              %p
                %strong From String structures to Spin structures on loop spaces
              %p
                %br/
              %p Ph.D. thesis,
              %p Università degli Studi Roma Tre, Rome, April 2016
              %p
                %br/
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://www.matfis.uniroma3.it/Allegati/Dottorato/TESI/capotosti/PhD%20Thesis%202016%20A%20Capotosti.pdf"}> thesis pdf
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Capotosti-FromStringStructures.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                talk slides
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Capotosti-FromStringStruc-Slides.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+string+structures"} differential string structures
          %p
            %strong Summary
          %p
            This thesis derives the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
            map of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+structures"} String structures
            on an
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 3
            ) to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin+structures"} Spin structures
            on its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
            from the existence of a natural morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-stacks"}
              smooth
              = succeed "-stacks" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}Spin
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbf{B}^2\big(\mathbf{B}U(1)_{conn}\big)
          %p
            refining the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+fractional+Pontryagin+class"} first fractional Pontryagin class
            (following
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Cech+Cocycles+for+Differential+characteristic+Classes"} Fiorenza, Schreiber and Stasheff 2012
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"} Konrad Waldorf
            in a series of papers.
          %p
            Recall that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin+manifold"} Spin manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is endowed with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+structure"} String structure
            if the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %mi X
                  %mi B
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 1
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \overset{f_{T X}}\rightarrow B Spin(n) \overset{\frac{1}{2}p_1}\rightarrow K(\mathbb{Z}, 4)
            is homotopically trivial, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{T X}
            denotes the classifying map for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi TX
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{TX}
            can be lifted to a map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mi String
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to B String(n)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi String
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B String(n)
            is defined as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{2}p_1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/based+loop+space"} based loop space
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi String
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B String(n)
            one obtains the topological
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+group"} String group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi String
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi BString
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} String(n) = \Omega BString(n)
          %p
            Let now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}X
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+loop+space"} free loop space
            of the Spin manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}Spin(n)
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+group"} loop group
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin+group"} Spin group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(n)
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is naturally an
            = succeed "-manifold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}Spin(n)
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite-dimensional+manifold"} infinite dimensional one
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T (\mathcal{L}X)
            is naturally associated with an
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}Spin(n)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}X
            (see
            %a{:href => "#smooth+loop+space#Waldorf11"} Waldorf 2011, Lemma 5.1
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "smooth+loop+space#SperaWurzbacher07"} Spera &amp; Wurzbacher 2007
          %p
            The loop group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}Spin(n)
            has a universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extension"} central extension
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ˜
                  %mo →
                  %mi LSpin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  1 \to U (1) \to\widetilde{\mathcal{L}Spin(n)} \to LSpin(n) \to 1
          %p
            and one defines a Spin structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}X
            as a lift of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+group"} structure group
            of the tangent bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T (\mathcal{L}X)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}X
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}Spin(n)
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi Spin
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde{\mathcal{L}Spin(n)}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T (\mathcal{L}X) \,\colon\, \mathcal{L}X \to B\mathcal{L}Spin(n)
            to a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ˜
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{L}X \to B\widetilde{\mathcal{L}Spin(n)}.
          %p
            Notice how a Spin structure on a loop space is not, strictly speaking a Spin structure, i.e., it is not a morphism to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi BSpin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi dim
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BSpin(dim \mathcal{L}X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}X
            is infinite dimensional, such a notion would be meaningless.
          %p
            It is well known in the theoretical physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folklore"} folklore
            that a String structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is essentially the same thing as a Spin structure on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mtext String structures on
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mtext Spin structures on
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{\text{String structures on}\;X\} \to \{\text{Spin structures on}\;\mathcal{L}X\},
          %p which induces a bijection at the level of isomorphism classes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mtext String structures on
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo ∼
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mtext Spin structures on
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo ∼
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{\text{String structures on}\;X\}/\sim \to \{\text{Spin structures on}\;\mathcal{L}X\}/\sim,
          %p
            as soon as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
          %p
            In this Thesis it is shown how the transgression map considered by Waldorf is naturally obtained from general constructions in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              \-category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-stacks"} smooth infinity-stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is compact and simply connected, and the latter result need to be proved by ad hoc methods.
          %p The crucial point in the stacky construction of the transgression map is the existence of a natural morphism of smooth stacks
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}Spin
                  \\longrightarrow
                  {\mathbf{B}}^2\big(\mathbf{B}U(1)_{conn}\big)
          %p
            refining the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+fractional+Pontryagin+class"} first fractional Pontryagin class
            %a{:href => "smooth+loop+space#Waldorf16"} Waldorf 2016
            in the form of a multiplicative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe"} bundle gerbe
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle+gerbe"} with connection
            over the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin+group"} Spin group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi Spin
                    %mo ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde{\mathcal{L}Spin}
            considered in the Thesis is what Waldorf calls a
            %em fusion extension
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi Spin
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}Spin
          %p
            But once the canonical multiplicative gerbe with connection over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi Spin
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B Spin
            is regarded as a morphism of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-stack"}
                smooth
                = succeed "-stacks" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi Spin
                    %mo ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde{\mathcal{L}Spin}
            is a fusion extension of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi Spin
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}Spin
            is encoded into the natural
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequence"} homotopy fiber sequence
            of smooth stacks
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mover
                            %mrow
                              %mi ℒ
                              %mi Spin
                            %mo ˜
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi ℒ
                          %mi Spin
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 2
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{B}\widetilde{\mathcal{L}Spin}
                  \&amp; \rightarrow &amp;
                  \\ast
                  \\\
                  \\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{B}\mathcal{L}Spin
                  \&amp;\rightarrow&amp;
                  \\mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
                  }
          %p
            induced by the morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}Spin \to {\mathbf{B}}^2\big({\mathbf{B}}U(1)_{conn}\big)
            and by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy"} holonomy
            morphism. Also, in the Thesis is provided a direct proof of the existence of the morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}Spin \rightarrow {\mathbf{B}}^2\big({\mathbf{B}}U(1)_{conn}\big)
            which does not rely on Waldorf’s result and is instead based on the differential refinement of the first fractional Pontryagin class
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi Spin
                    %mi conn
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 3
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac{1}{2} \hat{\mathbf{p}}_1
                  \\colon
                  \\mathbf{B}Spin_{conn} \to \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)_{conn}
          %p
            constructed in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Cech+Cocycles+for+Differential+characteristic+Classes"} Fiorenza, Schreiber and Stasheff 2012
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stringor+bundle"} stringor bundle
